From b7dafc945d2a4e5df3759f38aefe5cb098db9101 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Lemesre <eric.lemesre@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 08:37:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] feat(tools-pack): add .deb packaging target for linux
 build

`pnpm tools-pack linux build --to deb` produces a standards-compliant
Debian package, complementing the existing AppImage target. Answers the
README's deferral of .deb 'until there is demand and an owner'.

- config: accept `deb` for the linux `--to` target; CLI help updated.
- linux builder config (deb-scoped, no impact on AppImage/mac/win identity):
  Package `open-design`, install dir /opt/OpenDesign, /usr/bin/open-design,
  menu name 'Open Design', Section devel, Priority optional, RFC822 Maintainer,
  t64-aware Depends (+ libc6), Ayatana Recommends, Debian-standard filename.
- Debian packaging assets kept as files under resources/linux/debian/
  (DEP-5 copyright + changelog template), mirroring the maintainer convention.
- Verified: dpkg-deb + lintian (0 controllable-metadata tags; remainder is
  inherent Electron-bundle noise) + real boot.

Depends on the containerized-build fix (stacked).
